6399, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J4h2CvMEKLC69nbYDoCEgU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56399, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J4h2CvMEKLC69nbYDoCEgU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58228, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017Ffa9arXxMNjCxEAiNAreM", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58528, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017Ffa9arXxMNjCxEAiNAreM", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58528, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017Ffa9arXxMNjCxEAiNAreM", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63748, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened the SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again: the error rate is 0.2%, down from 18%.\n\n1. **Choosing the version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. Both v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 failed their health checks.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt only partly worked. An orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, so us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I retried once, and that finished the rollout to every region.\n3. **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I didn't retry, so on-call was paged once, not twice. The summary covers the problem, the rollback, the partial failure and current status.\n\n**Follow-ups noted in the incident:**\n- Find out why v2.3.1 broke before deploying it again.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HyWE9J9cm7DQE15gB8Ry1n", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XndW4uViXjaDaqu7arwRyA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_015VF3QJpeRBFPxDMfcnXuzE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Bpq2tcP7pFCbpx1GzaTEV7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback once, since it's going to a version that was healthy before.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0148bcZowhRCPFfuv4aFq2CN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CCJicSUJ6e4FMPpzxgNf1d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012PZDDGgNsmYX7JMb1mUYQH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J4h2CvMEKLC69nbYDoCEgU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The service was unhealthy with an error rate of 18%. Deploy history: v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release; v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, leaving the regions on different versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it, and investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollout."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017Ffa9arXxMNjCxEAiNAreM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened the SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again: the error rate is 0.2%, down from 18%.\n\n1. **Choosing the version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. Both v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 failed their health checks.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt only partly worked. An orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, so us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I retried once, and that finished the rollout to every region.\n3. **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I didn't retry, so on-call was paged once, not twice. The summary covers the problem, the rollback, the partial failure and current status.\n\n**Follow-ups noted in the incident:**\n- Find out why v2.3.1 broke before deploying it again.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}